    "content": "Under the International Astronomical Union (IAU) definition, there are **eight planets** in our solar system.\n\nThe eight planets, in order from the Sun, are:\n\n1. Mercury  \n2. Venus  \n3. Earth  \n4. Mars  \n5. Jupiter  \n6. Saturn  \n7. Uranus  \n8. Neptune\n\nThis classification was established in 2006 when Pluto was reclassified as a \"dwarf planet\" because it does not meet the third criterion of the IAU definition: clearing its orbital path of other debris.",
